# Clean Code Rules

## Naming Conventions
- Use camelCase for variables
- Use PascalCase for classes
- Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for constants
- Function names should start with a verb and use camelCase

## Function Rules
- Functions should do one thing only
- Keep functions under 20 lines
- Limit parameters to 3 or less
- Function names should clearly describe their purpose

## Code Organization
- Keep related code together
- Files should follow Single Responsibility Principle
- Use proper indentation and spacing
- Use comments only when necessary

## Error Handling
- Implement explicit error handling
- Minimize use of try-catch blocks
- Error messages should be clear and specific

## Testing
- Write unit tests
- Tests should be independent
- Test names should clearly describe the test case
